{"name":"Ocean Eyes","hex":"#a9c7cf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ocean eyes","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["blue eyes"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ocean_eyes"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ocean Eyes (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Ocean Eyes is the second studio album and major label debut by American electronica project Owl City, released on July 14, 2009, by Universal Republic Records. It features a photograph of the Burj Al Arab as its album artwork. A vinyl edition was released, followed by a deluxe edition available on January 26, 2010. The deluxe edition incorporates four new tracks, including a remix of \"Hello Seattle\". The album contains guest vocals by Relient K vocalist Matt Thiessen on the songs \"Fireflies\", \"Cave In\", \"The Bird and the Worm\", and \"Tidal Wave\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/79/Owl-city-ocean-eyes-2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ocean_Eyes_(album)","wikidata":"Q1947282"},{"title":"Ocean Eyes (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Ocean Eyes\" is the debut single by American singer-songwriter Billie Eilish. It was initially released on SoundCloud on November 18, 2015, and then temporarily released as a promotional recording on January 8, 2016, with Drup Music. \"Ocean Eyes\" was solely written and produced by Eilish's brother Finneas O'Connell, who originally wrote it for his band, but later gave the song to Eilish after feeling the song suited her vocals."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/ba/Billie_Eilish_-_Ocean_Eyes.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ocean_Eyes_(song)","wikidata":"Q30603613"},{"title":"Ocean","blocks":[{"text":"The ocean is the body of salt water that covers approximately 70.8% of Earth. The ocean is conventionally divided into large bodies of water, which are also referred to as oceans, and are themselves mostly divided into seas, gulfs, and subsequent bodies of water. The ocean contains 97% of Earth's water and is the primary component of Earth's hydrosphere, acting as a huge reservoir of heat for Earth's energy budget, as well as for its carbon cycle and water cycle, forming the basis for climate and weather patterns worldwide. The ocean is essential to life on Earth, harboring most of Earth's animals and protist life. It originated photosynthesis and therefore Earth's atmospheric oxygen, and still supplies half of it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Pacific_Ocean_as_viewed_from_GOES-18_on_September_23%2C_2023.jpg/330px-Pacific_Ocean_as_viewed_from_GOES-18_on_September_23%2C_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ocean","wikidata":"Q9430"},{"title":"Eye","blocks":[{"text":"An eye is a sensory organ that allows an organism to perceive visual information. It detects light and converts it into electro-chemical impulses in neurons (neurones). It is part of an organism's visual system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Krilleyekils.jpg/330px-Krilleyekils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye","wikidata":"Q7364"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e2/Billie_Eilish_-_Ocean_Eyes_%28Soundcloud%29.jpg/250px-Billie_Eilish_-_Ocean_Eyes_%28Soundcloud%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e2/Billie_Eilish_-_Ocean_Eyes_%28Soundcloud%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e2/Billie_Eilish_-_Ocean_Eyes_%28Soundcloud%29.jpg/250px-Billie_Eilish_-_Ocean_Eyes_%28Soundcloud%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABillie_Eilish_-_Ocean_Eyes_(Soundcloud).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/BillieEilishO2160622_%2845_of_45%29_%2852152978628%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-BillieEilishO2160622_%2845_of_45%29_%2852152978628%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/BillieEilishO2160622_%2845_of_45%29_%2852152978628%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-BillieEilishO2160622_%2845_of_45%29_%2852152978628%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/BillieEilishO2160622_%2845_of_45%29_%2852152978628%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-BillieEilishO2160622_%2845_of_45%29_%2852152978628%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Eilish performing \"Ocean Eyes\" as part of the Happier Than Ever, The World Tour (2022)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABillieEilishO2160622_(45_of_45)_(52152978628)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Mid-ocean_ridge_system.gif/500px-Mid-ocean_ridge_system.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Mid-ocean_ridge_system.gif/500px-Mid-ocean_ridge_system.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Bathymetry of the ocean floor showing the continental shelves and oceanic plateaus (red), the mid-ocean ridges (yellow-green) and the abyssal plains (blue to purple)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMid-ocean_ridge_system.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/NJ_LBI_Lighthouse_04.JPG/500px-NJ_LBI_Lighthouse_04.